        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d2b6a477-63be-5c85-978f-d989ae93d7e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, NASCAR Grand National races\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia, Middle Georgia Raceway\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series, race sponsorship, essay contests\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1966 and 1971, Middle Georgia Raceway hosted nine NASCAR Grand National races, a series now known as the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series.\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, the former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named the race after the winner of an essay contest held during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway Cup Series races each year, with the Toyota Owners 400 serving as the spring race.",
